{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And all the goods of his master in his hand.</b> This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 24:10): a deed of gift that he wrote for him, that all that is his is his, so that they would hasten to give him their daughter. And so in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 59:11): a deed. According to this opinion, the meaning of what is written (Genesis 25:5), \"And Abraham gave all that he had to Isaac,\" is to say that he invested him with the assets at the time of his passing so that they would not contest it, as it says, \"and he sent them away from upon Isaac his son while he was still alive.\" If so, the word of taking is drawn: \"and all the goods of his master in his hand\" — he took in his hand, or, \"and the servant took ten camels and all the goods of his master in his hand and went.\" And others explain that the servant, as soon as he swore, immediately went on his own and took ten camels from his master's camels, for all the goods of his master were in his hand, and he was the appointed officer over everything, to take from it whatever he wished, as it says (Genesis 24:2), \"who rules over all that he has.\" But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that the sense of this verse is like the sense of what is written concerning Hazael (II Kings 8:9), \"And Hazael went to meet him and took a gift in his hand, even all the goods of Damascus, the burden of forty camels\" — so too here it says that he took all the goods of his master in his hand as the burden of ten camels. And the meaning is that all the good and choice items of those kinds — fruits and delicacies of everything found in Damascus or in his master's house — they loaded as the camels' burden and brought a gift in their hand. And similarly (Genesis 45:23), \"ten donkeys carrying the best of Egypt\" — and the verses abbreviate their language in what is understood:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:33.485813897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}